<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — CaydexWidgets (app extension)

  REQUIRED TO UPLOAD, SEPARATELY FROM THE APP'S. Apple evaluates a required-reason API
  declaration per BINARY, and an app extension is its own binary inside the .ipa. The app
  target's manifest at `ios/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` does not cover this one; without this file
  the upload can fail ITMS-91053 naming CaydexWidgets specifically, which reads like an app
  problem and is not.

  This became necessary on 2026-09-07. The extension previously "performed no network call and
  held no credential" — it only read the App Group — and even then it used UserDefaults, so
  strictly it always needed a manifest. It now also authenticates a request with a widget token,
  which is why the omission was worth fixing rather than noting.

  Required-reason APIs: UserDefaults only. `UserDefaults(suiteName:)` in `WidgetAPIConfig`,
  `WidgetSnapshotStore` and `MoversConfigurationIntent` — all against the shared App Group
  `group.com.phan.caydex`, hence CA92.1 (access limited to the app group the process belongs
  to), not 1C8F.1. Verified ABSENT from `CaydexWidgets/` and `Shared/`: file-timestamp APIs,
  system boot time, disk space, and active-keyboard APIs.

  Tracking: false. The extension links no SDK at all — its only dependencies are WidgetKit,
  SwiftUI, AppIntents and Foundation.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is EMPTY, and that is a statement, not an oversight: the
  extension SENDS nothing about the user. Its one request carries a market-scoped widget token
  and returns a market-wide roll-up; it writes only to the shared container. Everything the app
  collects is declared in the app target's manifest, which is where it belongs — Apple merges
  the declarations across binaries, and restating them here would make the two drift.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- The App Group suite: the snapshot the app writes, the base-URL override,
			     the market/holdings mode toggle, and the widget token. Reads and writes
			     the shared container only — never the app's own defaults domain. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
